# Keeps the deployment source small.
#
# A CLI deploy uploads the working tree, and Next traces whatever it finds at
# the root into every serverless function. tmp/ alone is ~263mb of old audit
# artifacts, which is enough to blow the 250mb function limit on its own.
#
# This file controls what gets uploaded. It does not stop a build from being
# triggered in the first place: Vercel decides that from the push, before it
# reads anything here. The trigger filter is vercel.json's ignoreCommand, in
# scripts/vercel-ignore-build.mjs. The two are separate and both are needed.
#
# audits/ and artifacts/ are also gitignored now, so a git-based build never
# sees them either; they stay listed here for CLI deploys from a working tree
# that still has them on disk.
tmp
audits
artifacts
wiki
docs
tests
.next
.github
*.docx
*.pdf
*.jpg
!public/**/*.jpg
